{
  "name": "Google Drive to Instagram Reels",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Google Drive to Instagram Reels\n\n**What it does**\nDrop a finished vertical video into a Google Drive folder and it goes out as an Instagram Reel: the file is shared by link, an Instagram REELS container is created, the workflow waits until Instagram reports `FINISHED`, publishes it, and logs the permalink to Google Sheets. Failures go to Slack with the reason.\n\n**You need**\nAn Instagram professional account linked to a Facebook Page, a Meta app with a long-lived access token (instagram_basic, instagram_content_publish, pages_read_engagement), Google Drive, Google Sheets and Slack credentials.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Create a Facebook Graph API credential named `Meta Graph API account` with your token.\n2. Fill in **Settings** (Instagram user ID, size limit, hashtags) and pick the Drive folder.\n3. Activate, then drop a short MP4 (H.264, 9:16, under 50 MB) into the folder.\n\n**Keep files small.** A 54 MB Reel failed with \"Container Publication failed\" because the video fetch was rejected with HTTP 413. Compressing to about 5 MB fixed it:\n`ffmpeg -i in.mp4 -c:v libx264 -crf 28 -preset slow -c:a aac -b:a 128k -movflags +faststart out.mp4`\n\nBuilt by AI Strike Force, aistrikeforce.com",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 580
      },
      "id": "47cb8a00-7fac-5a06-86af-5b5e807a99d1",
      "name": "Google Drive to Instagram Reels",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -640,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
